  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Multisectoral Response to Humanitarian Needs of Afghan Returnees from Pakistan</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The main objective of this project is to contribute to addressing immediate post-arrival humanitarian needs of vulnerable returnees from Pakistan by providing cash-for-transportation, winterization support, and Camp Coordination and Camp Management (CCCM) services in their destination or place of origin. This IOM project provides activities such as the distribution of cash-for-transportation and conducting Post Distribution Monitoring (PDM), as well as others. The project provides life-saving assistance to 69,560 people, including 17,601 women, 22,049 men, 29,910 children, and 3,508 persons with disabilities.</narrative>
  </description>
